    "OtherAbstract": {
      "Type": "PIP",
      "Language": "eng",
      "AbstractText": "Irreversible hearing loss was observed in 4 women aged 19-42 years who had been treated with oral contraceptives for 8 months-10 years. Deafness progressed gradually in 2 cases, and occurred suddenly in 2 others; no predisposing conditions could be identified in any of the 4 patients. Oral contraceptives involved were Neorlest, Lyndiol, and Microgynon (1 patient each); the 4th patient had taken Sequilar, Microgynon, and Ediwal for periods of 1-4 months. Testing showed that the damage lay within the cochlea in all 4 cases. Thrombotic blockages of the blood vessels supplying the inner ear are discussed as pathophysiological mechanisms."
    }
  },
